#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 255 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Passes only float values through: any incoming float
is output unchanged \, while bangs \, symbols \, lists and any other
messages are silently ignored. Useful as a filter when a chain should
react only to numeric values.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Filtering a mixed stream — dropping non-numeric messages
(bangs \, symbols \, property messages) from a stream that mixes several
kinds of events \, so that only numbers reach the next object.;
#X text 250 248 • Protecting a numeric-only object — preventing a numeric
object (for example \, [mtof] \, [expr] \, [line]) from receiving unexpected
symbols or lists that would otherwise cause errors or unintended behavior.;
